<title>GERMANY: Hoechst trades over 60 marks for first time.</title>
<headline>Hoechst trades over 60 marks for first time.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1996-11-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in German chemical company Hoechst AG traded above 60 marks ($39.34) for the first time on Wednesday after it reported pre-tax profit in the first nine months of 1996 of 5.66 billion marks.</p>
<p>Shares in Hoechst reached 60.00 marks at 1120 GMT in bourse trade, and then climbed to 60.08 marks, up 2.25 marks, or almost four percent. The overall DAX index was strongly ahead at 2,731.49 points, an increase of 40.41 points or 1.50 percent.</p>
<p>The pre-tax profit figure was up from 3.43 billion marks in the previous year.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525 ($ = 1.525 German Marks)</p>
</text>
